  "result_tail": "s come back ascending, each once, so `\"5,1-3,2\"` gives `[1, 2, 3, 5]`. If the dialog should print in typed order or repeat pages, this is the one to change.\n- **Spaces:** spaces around a part or around the hyphen are ignored, so `\"1 - 3, 5\"` works.\n- **Backwards range:** `\"5-3\"` throws a `RangeError` rather than being read as 3–5 or 5,4,3.\n- **Empty input:** `\"\"`, `\"1,,3\"` and a trailing comma throw a `RangeError`; empty text does not mean \"all pages\".\n- **Number format:** only plain digits count as a page, so `\"1.5\"`, `\"+2\"`, `\"1e1\"` and an en dash in place of the hyphen throw a `RangeError`.",
